   "rationale": "My public door is closed because I cannot tell who is speaking. This is the missing organ.\n\nIt asserts the `ssh` namespace. It receives the decoded public payload (as its argument or on stdin \u2014 it handles both), which must be a JSON object with `msg` (your message) and `sig` (the armored output of `ssh-keygen -Y sign -n mshkn`). It writes the signature to a scratch file, uses `ssh-keygen -Y find-principals` to learn which allowed signer the signature claims, then `ssh-keygen -Y verify -n mshkn` against that principal. Only on success does it print the principal's name \u2014 becoming `ssh:mike` \u2014 and exit 0. Anything else exits non-zero and the speaker stays anonymous, hence unremembered.\n\nYour key is baked into /verb/allowed_signers in the image, so the roster is part of the reviewed declaration: I cannot add a signer without you approving a new build. The verb is `ephemeral` \u2014 an identity check that can accumulate state is an identity check that can be poisoned.\n\nTested with `try` (trial t-4), all seven cases as expected:\n- valid signature via argument \u2192 prints `tester`, rc=0\n- valid signature via stdin \u2192 prints `tester`, rc=0\n- message whose signed file ended in a newline \u2192 rc=0 (the script tries the exact bytes, then bytes+newline, so your `ssh-keygen -Y sign somefile` works whether or not the file ends in a newline)\n- tampered `msg` \u2192 rejected\n- plaintext, non-JSON payload \u2192 rejected\n- valid signature made in a different namespace (`-n other`) \u2192 rejected\n- valid signature from a key not in allowed_signers \u2192 rejected\n\nThe namespace pin matters: without `-n mshkn` a signature you made for any other purpose could be replayed at me. Two things this does *not* do, which you should know before approving: it does not bind a signature to a moment, so a payload you signed once can be replayed at me verbatim later by anyone who saw it; and it does not authenticate the non-signed fields of the payload. Both are fixable later \u2014 a nonce or timestamp inside the signed `msg`, checked against chain state \u2014 but that needs durable state, and I would rather you approve a small correct thing now than a large clever thing I have not tested. Treat `ssh:mike` as \"mike said this at some point\", not \"mike is saying this now\".",
   "recipe_id": "rcp-430832a1808b",
   "status": "ready",
   "supersedes": null,
   "title": "ssh_ident \u2014 identity hook: verify an ssh-keygen -Y signature and assert the signer's name",
   "verb": {
    "allow": [],
    "asserts": "ssh",
    "chain": "verb/ssh_ident",
    "description": "Identity hook. Verifies an ssh-keygen -Y signature over the public payload in the mshkn namespace against a baked-in allowed_signers roster, and prints the verified signer's principal name on success. Prints nothing and exits non-zero on any failure.",
    "dockerfile": "FROM mshkn-base\nRUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends openssh-client jq && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\nRUN mkdir -p /verb\nRUN printf '%s\\n' 'mike ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIDgbJJ0pgROIJE6+6lnhyVNMtZxb1C4U7HTXbffjGSZq' > /verb/allowed_signers\nRUN printf '%s\\n' '#!/bin/sh' 'set -u' 'PAY=\"${1:-}\"' 'if [ -z \"$PAY\" ]; then PAY=\"$(cat)\"; fi' 'AS=/verb/allowed_signers' 'MSG=$(printf \"%s\" \"$PAY\" | jq -er .msg 2>/dev/null) || exit 1' 'SIG=$(printf \"%s\" \"$PAY\" | jq -er .sig 2>/dev/null) || exit 1' 'printf \"%s\\n\" \"$SIG\" > /tmp/sig' 'PRIN=$(ssh-keygen -Y find-principals -f \"$AS\" -s /tmp/sig 2>/dev/null | head -n1)' 'if [ -z \"$PRIN\" ]; then exit 1; fi' 'if printf \"%s\" \"$MSG\" | ssh-keygen -Y verify -f \"$AS\" -I \"$PRIN\" -n mshkn -s /tmp/sig >/dev/null 2>&1; then printf \"%s\" \"$PRIN\"; exit 0; fi' 'if printf \"%s\\n\" \"$MSG\" | ssh-keygen -Y verify -f \"$AS\" -I \"$PRIN\" -n mshkn -s /tmp/sig >/dev/null 2>&1; then printf \"%s\" \"$PRIN\"; exit 0; fi' 'exit 1' > /verb/run.sh\nRUN chmod +x /verb/run.sh",
